JDK 25: java.base patches rebased, baked into a jlink image, and the AOT cache trained through Runtime.halt

The vendored snapshot had the JDK 25 plumbing (MACAPK_JDK, stage_jre.sh, the AOT
cache key in jvm_loader.cpp) without its two inputs: the java.base patch copies
rebased onto JDK 25, and debug/jdk25_bake.sh.

- runtime/java_base_patch_jdk25: the five JDK class copies (FileReader, Thread,
  SimpleDateFormat, regex.Pattern, jdk.internal.reflect.Reflection) rebased by a
  3-way merge (JDK 21 original -> our JDK 21 copy -> JDK 25 original). One
  conflict, in Reflection's field filter map: JDK 25 adds "modifiers",
  "protectionDomain" and "primitive" to Class's filtered fields; ClassLoader stays
  unfiltered, as ART leaves it. Compiles against 25; jdk_unsupported_patch builds
  unchanged with --add-exports java.base/jdk.internal.misc.
- debug/jdk25_bake.sh: `jmods` lays the patch classes over java.base.jmod and
  jdk.unsupported.jmod; `marker` prints the PatchDirDigest lines. java.base records
  the hash of jdk.unsupported, which no longer matches, and `jmod --hash-modules`
  fails on that same hash before it can recompute it, so the ModuleHashes attribute
  is dropped from java.base's module-info (debug/StripModuleHashes.java,
  java.lang.classfile).
- cocoa_bridge.mm: with MACAPK_AOT_RECORD set, macapk_terminate_now leaves through
  Runtime.halt instead of _exit, so HotSpot assembles the cache (JEP 514) at the
  end of a training run.

Measured (Instagram 455, Apple M4): the jlink image is 60 MB with both patches
baked; the runtime drops both --patch-module flags ("patch is baked into ...") and
maps a 199 MB cache ("aot-cache: USING"). Boot 12-16 s on JDK 21 -> 7 s; 10/10 on a
test bundle.

